.git
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
generated
**/generated
.turbo
coverage
**/coverage
*.log

# Uploaded files: they live in a volume at runtime (see docker-compose), so
# baking the local ones into the image would only ship stale files — including
# other people's deposit receipts.
apps/backend/uploads

# Secrets: never bake these into an image layer.
#
# The `**/` variants are NOT redundant: a bare `.env` pattern matches ONLY the
# context root, so apps/backend/.env, apps/web/.env and packages/database/.env
# were all being copied in (verified with `ls` inside the built image) —
# JWT_SECRET, NEXTAUTH_SECRET and the Pix key included. Every service gets its
# real values at RUNTIME via env_file/environment in docker-compose, so nothing
# needs them at build time.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
